{
  "dom_id": "step-q212984",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≡y-1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $0\\,R\\,8$\n\nII. $3\\,R\\,2$\n\nIII. $1\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,(-5)$",
  "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y-1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),$ or equivalently, $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $7∣(x-y+1).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $7∣(0-8+1),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. In this case, we have $7∣(3-2+1),$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $7∤(1-(-5)+1),$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
